# Public creation notes: 31f7f899

Canonical behavior identifies the unique fully occupied horizontal carrier,
measures each solid rectangular slot's height, sorts those input-derived heights
ascending, and redraws the same slot colors and widths from left to right. The
alternative sorts descending on the identical input stream. Step A's ordered
height vector is consumed by Step B's slot redraw; replacing that vector changes
the final grid.

The authoring grammar supports exact integer grids up to 30×30, repeated slot
colors, widths 1–3, odd and even heights, 3–9 bars, varied palettes and carrier
rows. The finite ten-profile bank has six demos and four shuffled queries. This
prototype is not owner-registered, qualified, accepted, or training-admitted.
